## Cloud Project Scouting Criteria

For AWS, Azure, GCP, Snowflake, and Databricks projects, the Scout Agent must classify each project as one of three types.

## Sandbox-First

Can run inside Atlas without credentials.

Examples:

> DuckDB simulates warehouse
> local dbt project
> fake S3 folder structure
> JSON IAM policy validation
> mock event stream
> local Spark-like fixture
> mock object storage
> local Delta/Iceberg-style table simulation

## BYO-Cloud Extension

Atlas gives optional real-cloud instructions.

Examples:

> Terraform template
> IAM least privilege
> cleanup script
> cost warning
> deployment checklist
> provider-specific setup guide

## Full Integration

Atlas directly connects to provider API.

This is future-only until credential safety is fully designed.

Full integration requires:

> encrypted credentials
> least-privilege scopes
> revocation flow
> no secrets in logs
> no secrets in Ada prompts
> cost controls
> resource tagging
> cleanup automation
> audit logging

